NEW INCIDENTS

PRIV-INC-MACSYNC-2026-09 =E2=80=94 CONFIRMED_MALICIOUS_CODE =E2=80=94 Evide=
nce B.
Kaspersky disclosed a newly observed September 2026 MacSync version on
17 September. The analyzed macOS infection chain delivers an
infostealer and persistent backdoor. Reported targets include saved
browser credentials, wallet-application data, macOS Keychain data,
device credentials and SSH/ZSH configuration. The backdoor can
remotely deploy modified browser add-ons and replace the legitimate
Ledger application with a malicious clone. No established aggregate
crypto loss was disclosed.

PRIV-INC-DCENT-APP-2026-09 =E2=80=94 SUSPICIOUS_UNVERIFIED =E2=80=94 Eviden=
ce C.
D=E2=80=99CENT/IoTrust publicly reported abnormal asset transfers involving
its App Wallet on 16 September and opened an investigation. Public
reporting limited the observed issue to the software App Wallet and
did not confirm an impact originating from D=E2=80=99CENT hardware wallets.
Independent XRPL analysis reported a large sweep, but ledger movement
alone was not accepted as proof that those wallets were compromised
through D=E2=80=99CENT. Root cause and accepted loss remained UNKNOWN.

MATERIAL UPDATES

No material upgrade to Needle was recorded.

REJECTED / DUPLICATE CLAIMS

Vite credential-harvesting reporting was treated as older activity
rather than a new hourly incident. Older Mastra, ChainDrop/Shai-Hulud
and related npm incidents were suppressed as historical/duplicate
cases.

TOP CASES FOR DEEP FORENSICS

PRIV-INC-DCENT-APP-2026-09 =E2=86=92 wallet/signer investigator: establish =
the
compromise mechanism and whether independent ledger observations can
be technically connected to the provider incident.

PRIV-INC-MACSYNC-2026-09 =E2=86=92 endpoint/key-authority investigator:
establish which wallet applications/extensions were demonstrably
